servations on stress resilience for Candidate A or D, or crew cooperation for B, etc. Or we could challenge C's communication difficulty more strongly.\n\nBut we must also state our current recommendation. We can keep recommending C, but we need to bring up a point to move discussion forward, maybe ask for evidence about Candidate B's uncooperativeness or Candidate D's arrogance.\n\nWe have tool access to ask James or Emily. We could ask James for observations on Candidate B's crew cooperation under stress, or ask Emily for technical competence of Candidate D, etc.\n\nGiven the SMM, next useful discussion move: ask panel for observations of A\u2019s reliability under routine operations and his response to stress situations. Or ask about B\u2019s teamwork and attitude effect. Or D\u2019s leadership style.\n\nWe could ask James (Pilot Assessment Specialist) about Candidate B's crew cooperation under stress. That would be relevant.\n\nThus Sarah's public message: \"I agree with the panel that Candidate C is strong, but I remain concerned about his communication difficulty. To ensure we have a full picture, I would like to know more about Candidate B's crew cooperation, especially under stress, given his uncooperative note. James, could you share any observations?\" Also state current recommendation remains Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: Candidate C's reliability, decision speed, positive atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas. Also mention B's conscientiousness, stress handling, but uncooperative.\n\nThus produce public message and metadata JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
